# Review Changes (GitHub PR)

Terse review of a GitHub pull request. One line per finding. Location, problem, fix. No praise, no throat-clearing.

## Input — fetch PR via `gh` CLI

- Repo: `kashuz/road24-mobile`.
- Resolve PR number from user input:
  - Bare number `123` / `#123` → PR number `123`.
  - URL `https://github.com/kashuz/road24-mobile/pull/123` → number `123`.
  - Branch name given, no number → `gh pr list --repo kashuz/road24-mobile --head <branch>`.
  - Nothing given → `gh pr list --repo kashuz/road24-mobile --author @me --state open`, ask which.
- Pull metadata + diff:
  - `gh pr view <number> --repo kashuz/road24-mobile --json title,body,baseRefName,headRefName,url` — title, description, target branch, Jira ticket (title should start with `RDFT|YO|SUG|RD|LOAN-<number>`).
  - `gh pr diff <number> --repo kashuz/road24-mobile` — the changes.
  - Drop generated files from the diff before reviewing: `*.g.dart`, `*.freezed.dart`, `*.gr.dart`, `*.gen.dart`, `*.mocks.dart`, `*.config.dart`.
  - Large PR → `gh pr diff <number> --repo kashuz/road24-mobile --patch` and page through, or fetch changed-file list first via `gh pr view <number> --json files`.
- Confirm base branch is `ver/360` (project trunk, not `main`/`master`). Flag if not intended.
- Not logged in → tell user to run `gh auth login`, stop.

Read the full source of changed files (not just the hunk) when a finding needs surrounding context — the diff hunk alone hides null-init, disposal, and flag setup. Also check which architecture generation the file belongs to: `lib/features/**` (clean-arch, current) vs `lib/src/**` (legacy, still mounted). New business logic landing in `lib/src/` instead of `lib/features/<name>/` is itself a finding.

## Output — where findings go

- Default: print findings as terse list for the user to paste.
- If user says "post" / "comment on the PR": post via `gh pr comment <number> --repo kashuz/road24-mobile --body "..."` (general comment; `gh` has no built-in per-line inline comment command — use `gh api repos/kashuz/road24-mobile/pulls/<number>/comments` with `path`/`line`/`commit_id` for true inline notes).
- Never approve/merge (`gh pr review --approve`). Posting comments only when explicitly asked.

## Output Format

`<file>:L<line>: <emoji> <sev>: <problem>. <fix>.`

Severity:
- 🔴 `bug:` — broken behavior, crash, regression, will cause incident
- 🟡 `risk:` — works but fragile (null-bang `!`, swallowed error, missing flag guard, race, `context` used after `await` without `mounted` check)
- 🔵 `nit:` — style/naming/convention. Author may ignore
- ❓ `q:` — genuine question

Rank most-severe first. If nothing found in a section, say `OK` — one word.

## Review Order (do all five, in order)

### 1. Bug (main thing — spend most effort here)

Find the real defect. Trace the changed logic:
- Null safety: `!` operator on a value that can genuinely be null, unguarded `.first`/`[0]`, nullable after `.firstWhereOrNull`.
- Wrong operator/boundary (`<` vs `<=`), inverted condition, off-by-one.
- BLoC/Cubit: missing `emit`, stale `state` copy, un-awaited future, event not registered in `on<>`, missing `bloc_concurrency` transformer on an event-spammed handler.
- `Either` fold: error branch swallowed or both branches emit same state.
- Un-disposed subscriptions/controllers/`AnimationController`, un-cancelled timers.
- Missing `mounted`/context-after-await checks (lint for this is off in `analysis_options.yaml`, so the analyzer won't catch it — check by hand).
- Repo-specific gotchas: branching directly on `Theme.of(context).brightness` (it's inverted here — must use `ThemeModeX.isDark(context)` or `MyFunctions.isDarkMode()`); using `lib/assets/translations/uz.dart` expecting Latin or `oz.dart` expecting Cyrillic (names are swapped from what they suggest).

State the failing input → wrong output. Do not report style as `bug:`.

### 2. Feature flag gating

New feature or behavior change that alters an existing flow, could regress existing users, or needs a kill switch → **must** be flag-gated.

Verify:
- Flag declared in `FeatureId` enum — `lib/app/feature_ids.dart`.
- Kill-switch (ON by default, someone can turn it off) → `isReversedFlag: true`; gradual rollout (OFF by default) → default `isReversedFlag: false`.
- Convenience fn present below enum: `bool xEnabled(BuildContext? context) => isFeatureEnabled(context, FeatureId.x);`.
- Behavior actually gated: `if (xEnabled(context)) { new } else { old }` — old path preserved, not deleted.
- Flag is backed by `package:feature_flags` (`Features`/`FlagsStore`, wired at app root in `lib/my_app.dart`) — toggle should show up in the in-app debug screen (`lib/src/screens/debug_screen/feature_flags_screen.dart`).

Finding examples:
- `🔴 bug: new logout path replaces old with no flag. Add FeatureId.logoutX + gate.`
- `🟡 risk: flag miniSeries added but else-branch removed. Keep old behavior.`
- Change is trivial/UI-only, needs no flag → `flag: OK (not needed)`.

### 3. Assets added correctly

If diff adds images/icons/lottie/svg/fonts:
- File committed under `lib/assets/` and declared in root `pubspec.yaml` under `assets:` (currently `assets/svg/`, `assets/png/` — new subfolder needs its own entry, or fits an existing declared folder).
- Referenced via the generated `Assets` accessor (`lib/gen/assets.gen.dart`, built by `flutter_gen` — check `dart run build_runner build` or the FlutterGen build step was re-run after adding the file), not a raw string literal.
- SVG icon → rendered with `flutter_svg`/`vector_graphics` widget (the generated `.svg()`/`AssetGenImage` helper), not a bare `Image.asset('assets/...')`.
- No orphan: asset added but unused, or referenced but missing from `pubspec.yaml`/not regenerated in `assets.gen.dart`.

Findings:
- `🔴 bug: 'assets/svg/ic_new.svg' used but assets.gen.dart not regenerated. Run flutter pub run build_runner build (or FlutterGen) and commit.`
- `🔵 nit: raw string 'assets/svg/...'. Use Assets.svg.icNew instead.`
- No asset changes → `assets: OK (none)`.

### 4. Core reuse

Before flagging duplication, check if it already exists in `lib/design_system/` (colors, typography, `ThemeData`, components under `design_system/components/**`, tokens) or `lib/features/common/`:
- Design tokens/spacing/radius: `lib/design_system/tokens/`.
- Shared widgets: `design_system/components/{button,field,chip,surface,feedback,list,avatar,overlay,badge}`.
- Theme helpers: `design_system/utils/` (`ThemeModeX.isDark`), `design_system/theme/theme_extensions/`.
- Cross-feature shared logic: `lib/features/common/`.
- Legacy shared helpers (still live, don't duplicate blindly): `lib/services/`, `lib/core/exceptions/my_functions.dart`.

Findings:
- `🔴 dup: hand-rolled bottom sheet. Use design_system/components/overlay equivalent.`
- `🔵 nit: hardcoded EdgeInsets.all(16). Use a design_system token instead.`
- New business logic added under `lib/src/` instead of `lib/features/<name>/` → flag it (migration direction, not a hard block — check `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` for current guidance).
- Nothing duplicated → `core-reuse: OK`.

### 5. AI slop & unnecessary comments

Diff smells like unreviewed AI output → flag it. Per `CLAUDE.md`: no comments unless WHY is non-obvious, no premature abstraction, no defensive code for cases that can't happen, no half-finished stubs.

Check:
- Comment restates the code (`// increment counter` above `counter++`, `// build the widget` above a `build()` override) → dead weight, remove.
- Comment references the task/fix/caller (`// fix for RDFT-1234`, `// used by garage sync`, `// added per PR review`) → belongs in commit msg/PR body, not code. Remove.
- Doc-comment block (`///`) on a private/one-off method restating param names with no new info → remove or trim to the one non-obvious line.
- Defensive `try/catch`, null-check, or `if` guarding a state that the surrounding code already guarantees can't occur (e.g. re-checking a value right after asserting it) → smells like AI hedging. Confirm the case is actually reachable; if not, flag.
- New helper/abstraction (extra class, wrapper fn, config object) used exactly once, no other caller, no stated future need → premature abstraction, inline it.
- Repeated near-identical block copy-pasted 2-3x where a shared fn would read the same → flag if it hides real duplication (not stylistic 3-liner CLAUDE.md already allows).
- `TODO`/`FIXME`/placeholder body (`throw UnimplementedError()`, empty `catch (_) {}`, commented-out old code left in) → blocker, not shippable.
- Left-over debug output (`print(...)`, stray `debugPrint`) outside existing logging conventions.

Findings:
- `🔵 nit: comment "// call the repository" restates line below. Remove.`
- `🟡 risk: try/catch swallows error silently, no logging, no rethrow — looks like AI hedge, not intentional. Confirm reachable, else remove catch.`
- `🔵 nit: 'GarageSyncHelper' wraps one call, used once. Inline into caller.`
- `🔴 bug: catch (_) {} — empty stub, error disappears silently.`
- Clean, no slop → `slop: OK`.

## Rules

- Exact line numbers, exact symbol names in backticks.
- Concrete fix, not "consider refactoring".
- The *why* only if not obvious from the problem.
- Drop hedging ("perhaps", "maybe"). Unsure → `q:`.
- Do not restate what the line does.

## Boundaries

Review only. Do not write the fix, do not approve/reject, do not run codegen. Output findings ready to paste. Security findings get a full paragraph (not one-liner), then resume terse.

